# Line-ending policy.
#
# The package is used on Windows and on Linux/WSL.  A CRLF in a `.py`/`.sh`
# file breaks a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang (`bash\r`) and makes a file's
# bytes depend on the local `core.autocrlf` checkout setting.  Pin LF for
# every text file that is executed, independent of that setting.
* text=auto
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts that must never be touched by the eol filter.
*.npz binary
*.npy binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webp binary
